IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa5-quoted-company-pay.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 10, Chapter 4A, "Directors of quoted companies ...: special provision": ss 226A to 226F
-- (lines 2949-3027 of ukpga-2006-46.txt): key definitions (s 226A), restrictions on remuneration and loss of office payments (ss 226B, 226C),
-- their supplementary rules (s 226D), civil consequences (s 226E) and the relationship with Chapter 4 (s 226F).
-- Whether a company is a "quoted company" is Part 15's answer (s 385, coa8): an input here, `s 385 the company is a quoted company`.
--
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text. The text shows ellipses
-- where words were repealed ("a quoted company ..."); they are read as absent.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa5-loans-exceptions.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING as the rule of 2026-10-29 reads them).

§ `Chapter 4A: directors of quoted companies (ss 226A to 226F)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 226A Key definitions
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2954 | “ quoted company ” has the same meaning as in Part 15 of this Act;
@ref s 226A(1) "quoted company" (src:2954-2954)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` MEANS `s 385 the company is a quoted company` -- "has the same meaning as in Part 15 of this Act": Part 15's answer, passed through unchanged

-- src:2961 | “ payment for loss of office ” has the same meaning as in Chapter 4 of this Part.
@ref s 226A(1) "payment for loss of office" (src:2961-2961)
GIVEN `s 215(1) the payment is a payment for loss of office` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(1) the payment is a payment for loss of office in this Chapter` MEANS `s 215(1) the payment is a payment for loss of office` -- "has the same meaning as in Chapter 4 of this Part": s 215(1)'s answer, passed through unchanged

DECLARE `s 226A(1) consideration for which the payment is made` IS ONE OF
    `s 226A(1)(a) holding, agreeing to hold or having held office as director of a company`
    `s 226A(1)(b)(i) holding, agreeing to hold or having held any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company`
    `s 226A(1)(b)(ii) holding, agreeing to hold or having held any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of a subsidiary undertaking of the company`
    `s 226A(1) something else`

-- src:2955 | “ remuneration payment ” means any form of payment or other benefit made to or otherwise conferred on a person as consideration for the person—
-- src:2956 | (a) holding, agreeing to hold or having held office as director of a company, or
-- src:2957 | (b) holding, agreeing to hold or having held, during a period when the person is or was such a director—
-- src:2958 | (i) any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company, or
-- src:2959 | (ii) any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of any subsidiary undertaking of the company,
-- src:2960 | other than a payment for loss of office;
@ref s 226A(1) "remuneration payment" (src:2955-2960)
GIVEN consideration IS A `s 226A(1) consideration for which the payment is made`
      `any form of payment or other benefit made to or otherwise conferred on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds or held the other office or employment during a period when the person is or was a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 226A(1) the payment is a payment for loss of office in this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(1) the payment is a remuneration payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `any form of payment or other benefit made to or otherwise conferred on a person`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“remuneration payment” means any form of payment or other benefit made to or otherwise conferred on a person"
        IF `s 226A(1) the payment is a payment for loss of office in this Chapter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a payment for loss of office"
        IF `s 226A(1) the payment is a payment for loss of office in this Chapter` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the payment is a payment for loss of office is s 215(1)'s answer
        IF consideration EQUALS `s 226A(1)(a) holding, agreeing to hold or having held office as director of a company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (consideration EQUALS `s 226A(1)(b)(i) holding, agreeing to hold or having held any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company`
            OR consideration EQUALS `s 226A(1)(b)(ii) holding, agreeing to hold or having held any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of a subsidiary undertaking of the company`)
           AND `the person holds or held the other office or employment during a period when the person is or was a director`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any form of payment or other benefit ... as consideration for the person— (a) holding, agreeing to hold or having held office as director of a company, or (b) holding, agreeing to hold or having held, during a period when the person is or was such a director— ..."

-- src:2953 | “directors' remuneration policy” means the policy of a quoted company... with respect to the making of remuneration payments and payments for loss of office;
@ref s 226A(1) "directors' remuneration policy" (src:2953-2953)
GIVEN `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the policy is the policy of the company with respect to the making of remuneration payments and payments for loss of office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(1) the policy is a directors' remuneration policy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is Part 15's answer
        IF `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the policy is the policy of the company with respect to the making of remuneration payments and payments for loss of office`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“directors' remuneration policy” means the policy of a quoted company ... with respect to the making of remuneration payments and payments for loss of office"

DECLARE `s 226A(4) transfer` IS ONE OF
    `s 226A(4)(a) a transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of the company or a subsidiary of the company`
    `s 226A(4)(b) a transfer of shares in the company, or in a subsidiary of the company, resulting from a takeover bid`
    `s 226A(4) some other transfer`

-- src:2972 | (4) In subsection (2), “ relevant transfer ” means—
-- src:2973 | (a) a transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of the company or a subsidiary of the company;
-- src:2974 | (b) a transfer of shares in the company, or in a subsidiary of the company, resulting from a takeover bid.
@ref s 226A(4) "relevant transfer" (src:2972-2974)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 226A(4) transfer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(4) the transfer is a relevant transfer` MEANS
    CONSIDER transfer
    WHEN `s 226A(4) some other transfer` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant transfer” means— (a) a transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property ...; (b) a transfer of shares"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2963 | (2) Subsection (3) applies where, in connection with a relevant transfer, a director of a quoted company ... is—
-- src:2964 | (a) to cease to hold office as director, or
-- src:2965 | (b) to cease to be the holder of—
-- src:2966 | (i) any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company, or
-- src:2967 | (ii) any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of any subsidiary undertaking of the company.
@ref s 226A(2) when subsection (3) applies (src:2963-2967)
GIVEN `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 226A(4) the transfer is a relevant transfer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a director of the quoted company is to cease to hold office as director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a director of the quoted company is to cease to be the holder of any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company or of a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(2) subsection (3) applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 226A(4) the transfer is a relevant transfer` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is quoted (Part 15) or the transfer is relevant is not known
        IF `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 226A(4) the transfer is a relevant transfer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND (`a director of the quoted company is to cease to hold office as director` OR `a director of the quoted company is to cease to be the holder of any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company or of a subsidiary undertaking`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (3) applies where, in connection with a relevant transfer, a director of a quoted company ... is— (a) to cease to hold office as director, or (b) to cease to be the holder of"

-- src:2969 | (a) the price to be paid to the director for any shares in the company held by the director is in excess of the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of like shares, or
@ref s 226A(3)(a) excess price for shares (src:2969-2969)
GIVEN `s 226A(2) subsection (3) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the price to be paid to the director for shares in the company held by the director` IS A NUMBER
      `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of like shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 226A(3)(a) the excess taken to have been a payment for loss of office for section 226C` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 226A(2) subsection (3) applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether subsection (3) applies is not known
        IF `s 226A(2) subsection (3) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (3) applies where"
        IF `the price to be paid to the director for shares in the company held by the director` GREATER THAN `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of like shares`
        THEN JUST (`the price to be paid to the director for shares in the company held by the director` MINUS `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of like shares`)
        OTHERWISE JUST 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If in connection with the transfer— (a) the price to be paid to the director for any shares in the company held by the director is in excess of the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of like shares" (no excess, so nothing is taken to be a payment)

-- src:2970 | (b) any valuable consideration is given to the director by a person other than the company,
-- src:2971 | the excess or, as the case may be, the money value of the consideration is taken for the purposes of section 226C to have been a payment for loss of office.
@ref s 226A(3)(b) valuable consideration given by another person (src:2970-2971)
GIVEN `s 226A(2) subsection (3) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `valuable consideration is given to the director by a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money value of the consideration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 226A(3)(b) the money value taken to have been a payment for loss of office for section 226C` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 226A(2) subsection (3) applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether subsection (3) applies is not known
        IF `s 226A(2) subsection (3) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (3) applies where"
        IF `valuable consideration is given to the director by a person other than the company`
        THEN JUST `the money value of the consideration`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any valuable consideration is given to the director by a person other than the company"

-- src:2975 | (5) References in this Chapter to the making of a remuneration payment or to the making of a payment for loss of office are to be read in accordance with this section.
@ref s 226A(5) references to the making of a payment (src:2975-2975)
GIVEN `the reference is to the making of a remuneration payment or to the making of a payment for loss of office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(5) the reference is read in accordance with section 226A` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to the making of a remuneration payment or to the making of a payment for loss of office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References in this Chapter to the making of a remuneration payment or to the making of a payment for loss of office are to be read in accordance with this section"

-- src:2976 | (6) References in this Chapter to a payment by a company include a payment by another person at the direction of, or on behalf of, the company.
@ref s 226A(6) payment by a company (src:2976-2976)
GIVEN `the payment is made by another person at the direction of, or on behalf of, the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(6) the payment is treated as a payment by the company` MEANS
    IF `the payment is made by another person at the direction of, or on behalf of, the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this Chapter to a payment by a company include a payment by another person at the direction of, or on behalf of, the company"

DECLARE `s 226A(7) the recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 226A(7)(a) a person connected with B`
    `s 226A(7)(b) a person at the direction of, or for the benefit of, B or a person connected with B`
    `s 226A(7) B himself`
    `s 226A(7) someone else`

-- src:2977 | (7) References in this Chapter to a payment to a person (“B”) who is, has been or is to be a director of a company include—
-- src:2978 | (a) a payment to a person connected with B, or
-- src:2979 | (b) a payment to a person at the direction of, or for the benefit of, B or a person connected with B.
@ref s 226A(7) payment to a connected person or at the direction of the director (src:2977-2979)
GIVEN recipient IS A `s 226A(7) the recipient`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(7) the payment is treated as a payment to B who is, has been or is to be a director` MEANS
    CONSIDER recipient
    WHEN `s 226A(7)(a) a person connected with B` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 226A(7)(b) a person at the direction of, or for the benefit of, B or a person connected with B` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 226A(7) B himself` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a payment to B himself is a payment to B without this subsection
    WHEN `s 226A(7) someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include— (a) a payment to a person connected with B, or (b) a payment to a person at the direction of, or for the benefit of, B"

-- src:2980 | (8) Section 252 applies for the purposes of determining whether a person is connected with a person who has been, or is to be, a director of a company as it applies for the purposes of determining whether a person is connected with a director.
@ref s 226A(8) connected persons (src:2980-2980)
GIVEN `the person has been, or is to be, a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(8) section 252 applies to determine whether a person is connected with the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has been, or is to be, a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who has been, or is to be, a director of a company"

DECLARE `s 226A(9) reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 226A(9) a reference to a director`
    `s 226A(9) a reference to loss of office as a director`

-- src:2981 | (9) References in this Chapter to a director include a shadow director but references to loss of office as a director do not include loss of a person's status as a shadow director.
@ref s 226A(9) shadow directors (src:2981-2981)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 226A(9) reference`
      `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(9) the reference includes the shadow director` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `s 226A(9) a reference to loss of office as a director` THEN
         IF `s 251 the person is a shadow director` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to loss of office as a director do not include loss of a person's status as a shadow director"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "references to loss of office as a director do not include loss of a person's status as a shadow director"
    WHEN `s 226A(9) a reference to a director` THEN
         CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this Chapter to a director include a shadow director"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a shadow director is s 251's answer

-- (a) of subsection (10): "its chief executive officer (however described)"; (b) and the words after (a) are shown as dots (repealed or blank in this text).
-- src:2982 | (10) References in this Chapter (other than sections 226E(2)(b) and (5)) to a director of a company include a person who is not a director of the company but who is—
-- src:2983 | (a) its chief executive officer (however described),...
-- src:2984 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 226A(10) the chief executive officer (src:2982-2984)
GIVEN `the person is not a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is its chief executive officer (however described)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in section 226E(2)(b) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226A(10) the reference to a director includes the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the reference is in section 226E(2)(b) or (5)`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References in this Chapter (other than sections 226E(2)(b) and (5))"
        IF `the person is not a director of the company` AND `the person is its chief executive officer (however described)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include a person who is not a director of the company but who is— (a) its chief executive officer (however described)"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 226B Remuneration payments, s 226C Loss of office payments
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2990 | (2) The approved directors' remuneration policy is the most recent remuneration policy to have been approved by a resolution passed by the members of the company in general meeting.
@ref s 226B(2) the approved directors' remuneration policy (src:2990-2990)
GIVEN `the policy was approved by a resolution passed by the members of the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no more recent remuneration policy has been so approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226B(2) the policy is the approved directors' remuneration policy` MEANS
    IF `the policy was approved by a resolution passed by the members of the company in general meeting` AND `no more recent remuneration policy has been so approved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The approved directors' remuneration policy is the most recent remuneration policy to have been approved by a resolution passed by the members of the company in general meeting"

-- src:2987 | (1) A quoted company ... may not make a remuneration payment to a person who is, or is to be or has been, a director of the company unless—
-- src:2988 | (a) the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy, or
-- src:2989 | (b) the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company.
@ref s 226B(1) remuneration payments (src:2987-2989)
GIVEN `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the payment is to a person who is, or is to be or has been, a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226B(1) the quoted company may not make the remuneration payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is Part 15's answer
        IF `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A quoted company ... may not make a remuneration payment"
        IF NOT `the payment is to a person who is, or is to be or has been, a director of the company`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a remuneration payment to a person who is, or is to be or has been, a director of the company"
        IF `the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy` OR `the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless— (a) the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy, or (b) the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "A quoted company ... may not make a remuneration payment"

-- src:2995 | (2) The approved directors' remuneration policy is the most recent remuneration policy to have been approved by a resolution passed by the members of the company in general meeting.
@ref s 226C(2) the approved directors' remuneration policy (src:2995-2995)
GIVEN `the policy was approved by a resolution passed by the members of the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no more recent remuneration policy has been so approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226C(2) the policy is the approved directors' remuneration policy` MEANS
    IF `the policy was approved by a resolution passed by the members of the company in general meeting` AND `no more recent remuneration policy has been so approved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The approved directors' remuneration policy is the most recent remuneration policy to have been approved by a resolution passed by the members of the company in general meeting"

-- src:2992 | (1) No payment for loss of office may be made by any person to a person who is, or has been, a director of a quoted company ... unless—
-- src:2993 | (a) the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy, or
-- src:2994 | (b) the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company.
@ref s 226C(1) loss of office payments (src:2992-2994)
GIVEN `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the payment for loss of office is to a person who is, or has been, a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226C(1) no person may make the payment for loss of office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is Part 15's answer
        IF `s 226A(1) the company is a quoted company in this Chapter` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a director of a quoted company"
        IF NOT `the payment for loss of office is to a person who is, or has been, a director of the company`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person who is, or has been, a director of a quoted company"
        IF `the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy` OR `the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless— (a) the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy, or (b) the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "No payment for loss of office may be made by any person to a person who is, or has been, a director of a quoted company"

-- The duty twin (a trace cannot be asserted on the stable binary; the decision functions above carry the assertions).
DECLARE `s 226B action` IS ONE OF
    `s 226B make the remuneration payment or payment for loss of office`

-- src:2987 | (1) A quoted company ... may not make a remuneration payment to a person who is, or is to be or has been, a director of the company unless—
-- src:2988 | (a) the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy, or
-- src:2989 | (b) the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company.
-- src:2990 | (2) The approved directors' remuneration policy is the most recent remuneration policy to have been approved by a resolution passed by the members of the company in general meeting.
-- src:2991 | 226C Loss of office payments
-- src:2992 | (1) No payment for loss of office may be made by any person to a person who is, or has been, a director of a quoted company ... unless—
-- src:2993 | (a) the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy, or
-- src:2994 | (b) the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company.
@ref s 226B(1) and s 226C(1) the duty not to make the payment (src:2987-2994)
GIVEN `the bar applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 226B action`
`s 226B(1) and s 226C(1) the duty not to make the payment` MEANS
    IF `the bar applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Company
         SHANT `s 226B make the remuneration payment or payment for loss of office`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 226B or s 226C: a payment was made that is neither consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy nor approved by resolution of the members"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 226D Sections 226B and 226C: supplementary
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- "not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting": first day of inspection plus 14 days is not after the date of the meeting.
-- src:2997 | (1) A resolution approving a payment for the purposes of section 226B(1)(b) or 226C(1)(b) must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment ... (including its amount) is made available for inspection by the members of the company—
-- src:2998 | (a) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered, and
-- src:2999 | (b) at that meeting itself.
@ref s 226D(1) the memorandum (src:2997-2999)
GIVEN `the resolution approves a payment for the purposes of section 226B(1)(b) or 226C(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment (including its amount) is made available for inspection by the members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered` IS A DATE
      `it is available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226D(1) the resolution approving the payment must not be passed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the resolution approves a payment for the purposes of section 226B(1)(b) or 226C(1)(b)`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution approving a payment for the purposes of section 226B(1)(b) or 226C(1)(b)"
        IF `a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment (including its amount) is made available for inspection by the members`
           AND `the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` PLUS 14 AT MOST `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered`
           AND `it is available for inspection at the meeting itself`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be passed unless a memorandum ... is made available for inspection by the members of the company— (a) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting ..., and (b) at that meeting itself"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "must not be passed"

-- src:3000 | (2) The memorandum must explain the ways in which the payment is inconsistent with the approved directors’ remuneration policy (within the meaning of the section in question).
@ref s 226D(2) the memorandum must explain the inconsistency (src:3000-3000)
GIVEN `the memorandum explains the ways in which the payment is inconsistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226D(2) the memorandum meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the memorandum explains the ways in which the payment is inconsistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The memorandum must explain the ways in which the payment is inconsistent with the approved directors’ remuneration policy"

-- (7): "the company's website" is the website on which the company makes material available under s 430 (coa9).
-- src:3007 | (7) In this section the “company's website” is the website on which the company makes material available under section 430.
@ref s 226D(7) the company's website (src:3007-3007)
GIVEN `the website is the website on which the company makes material available under section 430` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226D(7) the website is the company's website` MEANS
    IF `the website is the website on which the company makes material available under section 430`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the “company's website” is the website on which the company makes material available under section 430"

-- (3): from the first day the memorandum is available for inspection until the next accounts meeting.
-- src:3001 | (3) The company must ensure that the memorandum is made available on the company's website from the first day on which the memorandum is made available for inspection under subsection (1) until its next accounts meeting.
@ref s 226D(3) the memorandum on the company's website (src:3001-3001)
GIVEN `the first day the memorandum was available for inspection under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the first day the memorandum was available on the company's website` IS A DATE
      `the last day the memorandum was available on the company's website` IS A DATE
      `the date of the company's next accounts meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226D(3) the company has ensured the memorandum is available on its website` MEANS
    IF `the first day the memorandum was available on the company's website` AT MOST `the first day the memorandum was available for inspection under subsection (1)`
       AND `the last day the memorandum was available on the company's website` AT LEAST `the date of the company's next accounts meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must ensure that the memorandum is made available on the company's website from the first day on which the memorandum is made available for inspection under subsection (1) until its next accounts meeting"

-- (The duty of (3) is a continuing duty with no act to be done by a time the text states: it is encoded as the decision function above only, and no
-- regulative rule is written for it so that no deadline is invented.)

-- src:3002 | (4) Failure to comply with subsection (3) does not affect the validity of the meeting at which a resolution is passed approving a payment to which the memorandum relates or the validity of anything done at the meeting.
@ref s 226D(4) validity of the meeting (src:3002-3002)
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226D(4) the failure affects the validity of the meeting or of anything done at it` MEANS
    IF `the company failed to comply with subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with subsection (3) does not affect the validity of the meeting at which a resolution is passed approving a payment to which the memorandum relates or the validity of anything done at the meeting"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Failure to comply with subsection (3)"

-- src:3003 | (5) Nothing in section 226B or 226C authorises the making of a remuneration payment or (as the case may be) a payment for loss of office in contravention of the articles of the company concerned.
@ref s 226D(5) the articles (src:3003-3003)
GIVEN `the payment is in contravention of the articles of the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226D(5) section 226B or 226C authorises the payment` MEANS
    IF `the payment is in contravention of the articles of the company concerned`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in section 226B or 226C authorises the making of a remuneration payment or (as the case may be) a payment for loss of office in contravention of the articles of the company concerned"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in contravention of the articles of the company concerned"

-- (6): before the earlier of (a) the end of the first financial year to begin on or after the day the company becomes a quoted company, and (b) the date from
-- which the company's first directors' remuneration policy approved under s 439A takes effect (an input; none yet: NOTHING).
-- src:3004 | (6) Nothing in section 226B or 226C applies in relation to a remuneration payment or (as the case may be) a payment for loss of office made to a person who is, or is to be or has been, a director of a quoted company ... before the earlier of—
-- src:3005 | (a) the end of the first financial year of the company to begin on or after the day on which it becomes a quoted company ..., and
-- src:3006 | (b) the date from which the company's first directors' remuneration policy to be approved under section 439A takes effect.
@ref s 226D(6) payments before the first policy (src:3004-3006)
GIVEN `the date of the payment` IS A DATE
      `the end of the first financial year of the company to begin on or after the day on which it becomes a quoted company` IS A DATE
      `the date from which the company's first directors' remuneration policy approved under section 439A takes effect` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226D(6) sections 226B and 226C apply to the payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date from which the company's first directors' remuneration policy approved under section 439A takes effect`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
         IF `the date of the payment` LESS THAN `the end of the first financial year of the company to begin on or after the day on which it becomes a quoted company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in section 226B or 226C applies ... before the earlier of— (a) the end of the first financial year ..."
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the earlier of" (on or after that day the subsection says nothing)
    WHEN JUST policyDate THEN
         IF `the date of the payment` LESS THAN `the end of the first financial year of the company to begin on or after the day on which it becomes a quoted company` AND `the date of the payment` LESS THAN policyDate -- before the earlier of the two dates: before each
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in section 226B or 226C applies ... before the earlier of— (a) the end of the first financial year ..., and (b) the date from which the company's first directors' remuneration policy ... takes effect"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the earlier of" (on or after the earlier date the subsection says nothing)

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 226E Payments made without approval: civil consequences
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3010 | (1) An obligation (however arising) to make a payment which would be in contravention of section 226B or 226C has no effect.
@ref s 226E(1) an obligation to make the payment has no effect (src:3010-3010)
GIVEN `the obligation is to make a payment which would be in contravention of section 226B or 226C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226E(1) the obligation has effect` MEANS
    IF `the obligation is to make a payment which would be in contravention of section 226B or 226C`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An obligation (however arising) to make a payment which would be in contravention of section 226B or 226C has no effect"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to make a payment which would be in contravention of section 226B or 226C"

DECLARE `s 226E for whom the payment is held on trust` IS ONE OF
    `s 226E(2)(a) the company or other person making the payment`
    `s 226E(3)(b) the company whose undertaking or property is or is proposed to be transferred`
    `s 226E(4)(b) the persons who have sold their shares as a result of the offer made`

DECLARE `s 226E kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 226E(2) a payment in contravention of section 226B or 226C (neither (3) nor (4) applies)`
    `s 226E(3) a payment for loss of office in contravention of section 226C to a director of a quoted company in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property of the company or a subsidiary`
    `s 226E(4) a payment for loss of office in contravention of section 226C to a director of a quoted company in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid`
    `s 226E some other payment`

-- src:3011 | (2) If a payment is made in contravention of section 226B or 226C—
-- src:3012 | (a) it is held by the recipient on trust for the company or other person making the payment, and
-- src:3013 | (b) in the case of a payment by a company, any director who authorised the payment is jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company that made the payment for any loss resulting from it.
-- src:3014 | (3) If a payment for loss of office is made in contravention of section 226C to a director of a quoted company ... in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of the company or a subsidiary of the company—
-- src:3015 | (a) subsection (2) does not apply, and
-- src:3016 | (b) the payment is held by the recipient on trust for the company whose undertaking or property is or is proposed to be transferred.
-- src:3017 | (4) If a payment for loss of office is made in contravention of section 226C to a director of a quoted company ... in connection with a transfer of shares in the company, or in a subsidiary of the company, resulting from a takeover bid—
-- src:3018 | (a) subsection (2) does not apply,
-- src:3019 | (b) the payment is held by the recipient on trust for persons who have sold their shares as a result of the offer made, and
-- src:3020 | (c) the expenses incurred by the recipient in distributing that sum amongst those persons shall be borne by the recipient and not retained out of that sum.
@ref s 226E(2) to (4) for whom the payment is held on trust (src:3011-3020)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 226E kind of payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 226E for whom the payment is held on trust`
`s 226E the payment is held by the recipient on trust for` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 226E(2) a payment in contravention of section 226B or 226C (neither (3) nor (4) applies)` THEN JUST `s 226E(2)(a) the company or other person making the payment`
    WHEN `s 226E(3) a payment for loss of office in contravention of section 226C to a director of a quoted company in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property of the company or a subsidiary` THEN JUST `s 226E(3)(b) the company whose undertaking or property is or is proposed to be transferred` -- (3)(a): subsection (2) does not apply
    WHEN `s 226E(4) a payment for loss of office in contravention of section 226C to a director of a quoted company in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid` THEN JUST `s 226E(4)(b) the persons who have sold their shares as a result of the offer made` -- (4)(a): subsection (2) does not apply
    WHEN `s 226E some other payment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a payment is made in contravention of section 226B or 226C"

-- src:3013 | (b) in the case of a payment by a company, any director who authorised the payment is jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company that made the payment for any loss resulting from it.
@ref s 226E(2)(b) the authorising director's liability (src:3013-3013)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 226E kind of payment`
      `the payment is by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director authorised the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226E(2)(b) the director is jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company that made the payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS `s 226E some other payment`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a payment is made in contravention of section 226B or 226C"
        IF kind EQUALS `s 226E(3) a payment for loss of office in contravention of section 226C to a director of a quoted company in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property of the company or a subsidiary` OR kind EQUALS `s 226E(4) a payment for loss of office in contravention of section 226C to a director of a quoted company in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) subsection (2) does not apply" (subsections (3) and (4))
        IF `the payment is by a company` AND `the director authorised the payment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the payment is by a company`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any director who authorised the payment"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a payment by a company"

-- src:3017 | (4) If a payment for loss of office is made in contravention of section 226C to a director of a quoted company ... in connection with a transfer of shares in the company, or in a subsidiary of the company, resulting from a takeover bid—
-- src:3018 | (a) subsection (2) does not apply,
-- src:3019 | (b) the payment is held by the recipient on trust for persons who have sold their shares as a result of the offer made, and
-- src:3020 | (c) the expenses incurred by the recipient in distributing that sum amongst those persons shall be borne by the recipient and not retained out of that sum.
@ref s 226E(4)(c) the recipient's expenses of distribution (src:3017-3020)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 226E kind of payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226E(4)(c) the expenses incurred by the recipient in distributing the sum are borne by the recipient and not retained out of the sum` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `s 226E(4) a payment for loss of office in contravention of section 226C to a director of a quoted company in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in connection with a transfer of shares in the company, or in a subsidiary of the company, resulting from a takeover bid"

-- (5): the court may relieve a director from liability under (2)(b) wholly or in part if he shows he acted honestly and reasonably and the court considers he ought to be relieved.
-- src:3021 | (5) If in proceedings against a director for the enforcement of a liability under subsection (2)(b)—
-- src:3022 | (a) the director shows that he or she has acted honestly and reasonably, and
-- src:3023 | (b) the court considers that, having regard to all the circumstances of the case, the director ought to be relieved of liability,
-- src:3024 | the court may relieve the director, either wholly or in part, from liability on such terms as the court thinks fit.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (name-test sweep, fork F-NT-226E5): the function is named for a power or grant given "if" a gate is met (no "only if"); when the gate fails the answer is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE. The other reading, a failed "if" read as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE.
@ref s 226E(5) relief of a director (src:3021-3024)
GIVEN `in proceedings for the enforcement of a liability under subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director shows that he or she has acted honestly and reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers that, having regard to all the circumstances, the director ought to be relieved of liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226E(5) the court may relieve the director from liability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `in proceedings for the enforcement of a liability under subsection (2)(b)`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If in proceedings against a director for the enforcement of a liability under subsection (2)(b)"
        IF `the director shows that he or she has acted honestly and reasonably` AND `the court considers that, having regard to all the circumstances, the director ought to be relieved of liability`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If ... (a) the director shows that he or she has acted honestly and reasonably, and (b) the court considers that ... the director ought to be relieved of liability, the court may relieve the director" (this subsection gives the court no power on these facts)

